# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  CSV → Personalized Email Generator — environment
#  Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.  NEVER commit `.env.local`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── App ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL: run `npm run db:start`, then copy the values it prints.
# CLOUD: Project Settings → API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:54321"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="<copy from `npm run db:start` output>"

# ── Postgres ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two connection strings, and the difference matters:
#
#   DATABASE_URL  runtime queries.  On Supabase Cloud use the POOLED
#                 (Supavisor, transaction mode) string on port 6543.
#                 Transaction pooling cannot use prepared statements —
#                 src/db/index.ts sets `prepare: false` for exactly this reason.
#
#   DIRECT_URL    migrations only.  Must be the DIRECT/session connection
#                 on port 5432.  DDL over a transaction pooler will fail
#                 in confusing, intermittent ways.
#
# Locally both point at the same Supabase container (port 54322).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres"

# ── Encryption ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Key-encryption key for Google refresh tokens and Anthropic API keys.
# 32 random bytes, base64. Generate with:  npm run keygen
# Rotating this invalidates every stored credential (users must reconnect).
ENCRYPTION_KEY="<npm run keygen>"

# Separate secret for signing one-click unsubscribe tokens (HMAC-SHA256).
# Generate with:  npm run keygen
UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET="<npm run keygen>"

# ── Google OAuth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID
# (Web application). Enable the Gmail API. Keep the consent screen in
# "Testing" mode and add yourself as a test user — no verification needed.
#
# Authorized redirect URIs must include BOTH:
#   http://127.0.0.1:54321/auth/v1/callback      (local Supabase)
#   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback   (cloud, when you deploy)
#
# Supabase performs the initial handshake; WE refresh the Gmail token ourselves,
# which is why the client secret is needed here too.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# ── Anthropic ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Intentionally absent. This is a bring-your-own-key application: each user
# pastes their own key in Settings → AI, and it is stored AES-256-GCM
# encrypted in the database. The app never ships a key and works fully in
# template-only mode without one.
